A couple of suggestions for new versions of nethack

- currently, nethack doesn't say you're unlucky on Friday the 13th. Maybe
you are, unknowingly. If not, this might be an addition - min. luck 2
points lower on Fr 13

- lightswitches
Some rooms have a light switch somewhere along the wall. You won't
automatically see it, you have to search for it. Turning the light switch
toggles the light/dark status of the room.
Applying a pick-axe to a section of the wall that has a light switch
results in an electric shock. Wand of digging ...
Shops may have a light switch in a particular place where one is likely
to try and hack through.
With high dexterity, one might disable a light switch using the Swiss
Army knife which will replace the tin-opener. Failure to disable the
light switch might result in electric shock, permanent darkness, loss of
the SA knife, ...

- the Swiss Army knife
Occasionally one might be able to retrieve a lost ring from a sink using
the SA knife. Of course, the knife might drop down the drain as well.
It is a minor weapon as well. Some dead monsters can be skinned using the
SA knife. It is an invaluable tool for opening some potions.

- red, pink and white potions
will become potions of wine-like nature. This implies that a mild
intoxication might result from quaffing them (booze can become stronger).
If one is marginally dexterous, quaffing such a potion is only possible
using a SA knife. Otherwise, the potion may get lost or become
cursed/cause sickness by pieces of cork that remain in the fluid.
Cursed/blessed wine potions ... (like tins?)

